                <pb facs="0143" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1131</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-21T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 21, 3.54
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul Harbin now telegraphs Japanese Consul there informs him Japan is preparing
                    military expedition to assist Russians to restore order in Siberia. Horvat also approached by agent of Japanese
                    Government with offer of assistance. Horvat, if assured of Allied support, is willing to avail
                    himself of leadership of conservative Russians in Siberia against Bolsheviks.
                        Horvat now on the way to Peking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Reinsch</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
